gain and again.'),(5902,'An Order...'),(5903,'Sale packing list lines are part of sale packing lists, and bear the different references that have been sold. For each product/service reference there will be a sale packing list line.'),(5904,'Une ligne tarifaire.'),(5905,'Sale Packing List allows for keeping a trace of goods or services which have been delivered to a customer. It can track how delivered goods or services differ from ordered goods or services. A single order may therefore result in multiple packing lists. Packing Lists directly impact the inventory. It is essential to understand that once an order has been confirmed, it should never be modified since it defines a contractual relation. Changes to initial expectations shall be entered into Packing Lists, not in Orders. The impact of changes shall be calculated automatically through so-called \"Solvers\" which postpone backordered goods, accept the changes to initial expectations, etc. based on standard or custom business rules.'),(5906,'An Order...'),(5907,'Sale order lines are part of sale orders and bear the different product or service references that have been sold by the company.'),(5908,'A DeliveryCell allows to define specific quantities for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5909,'When a user of ERP5 wants to materialize a sale that has been done by his company, he or she should use a sale order. Sale orders contain some general information about the buyer and the seller, and contain sale order lines.'),(5910,'Contains Returned Sale Packing List'),(5911,'Returned Sale Packing List Lines are part of returend sale packing lists and bear the different product or service references that are returned by the customer.'),(5912,'A Returned Sale Packing List Cell allows to define specific quantities for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5913,'Returned Sale Packing List allows for keeping a trace of goods or services which have been delivered to a customer. It can track how delivered goods or services differ from ordered goods or services. A single order may therefore result in multiple packing lists. Packing Lists directly impact the inventory. It is essential to understand that once an order has been confirmed, it should never be modified since it defines a contractual relation. Changes to initial expectations shall be entered into Packing Lists, not in Orders. The impact of changes shall be calculated automatically through so-called \"Solvers\" which postpone backordered goods, accept the changes to initial expectations, etc. based on standard or custom business rules.'),(5914,'An Order...'),(5915,'Sale order lines are part of sale orders and bear the different product or service references that have been sold by the company.'),(5916,'A DeliveryCell allows to define specific quantities for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5917,'When a user of ERP5 wants to materialize a sale that has been done by his company, he or she should use a sale order. Sale orders contain some general information about the buyer and the seller, and contain sale order lines.'),(5918,'A container of Returned Purchase Packing Lists.'),(5919,'Returned Purchase Packing List Lines are part of returned purchase packing lists and bear the different product or service references that are returned by the company.'),(5920,'A Returned Purchase Packing List Cell specifies a price and a quantity for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5921,'Returned Purchase Packing List allows for keeping a trace of goods or services which have been delivered to a customer. It can track how delivered goods or services differ from ordered goods or services. A single order may therefore result in multiple packing lists. Packing Lists directly impact the inventory. It is essential to understand that once an order has been confirmed, it should never be modified since it defines a contractual relation. Changes to initial expectations shall be entered into Packing Lists, not in Orders. The impact of changes shall be calculated automatically through so-called \"Solvers\" which postpone backordered goods, accept the changes to initial expectations, etc. based on standard or custom business rules.'),(5922,'Holds Returned Purchase Orders'),(5923,'Purchase order lines are part of purchase orders and bear the different product or service references that have been purchased by the company.'),(5924,'A DeliveryCell allows to define specific quantities for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5926,'Holds Purchase Trade Conditions'),(5927,'Purchase trade conditions are documents that gather all the details of a standard purchase order, such as the shipment or payment mode, the tax or discount behaviour. A purchase trade condition can be applied to a purchase order, and in this case, the information borne by the purchase trade condition will be imported to the purchase order. This is practical for the user, because it allows not to loose time typing the same information again and again.'),(5928,'Holds Purchase Packing Lists'),(5929,'Purchase packing list lines are part of purchase packing lists, and bear the different references that have been ordered. For each product/service reference there will be a purchase packing list line.'),(5930,'Une ligne tarifaire.'),(5931,'Purchase Packing List allows for keeping a trace of goods or services which have been received from a supplier. It can track how received goods or services differ from ordered goods or services. A single order may therefore result in multiple packing lists. Packing Lists directly impact the inventory. It is essential to understand that once an order has been confirmed, it should never be modified since it defines a contractual relation. Changes to initial expectations shall be entered into Packing Lists, not in Orders. The impact of changes shall be calculated automatically through so-called \"Solvers\" which postpone backordered goods, accept the changes to initial expectations, etc. based on standard or custom business rules.'),(5932,'Holds Purchase Orders'),(5933,'Purchase order lines are part of purchase orders and bear the different product or service references that have been purchased by the company.'),(5934,'A DeliveryCell allows to define specific quantities for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5935,'When a user of ERP5 wants to materialize a purchase that has been done by his company, he or she should use a purchase order. Purchase orders contain some general information about the buyer and the seller, and contain purchase order lines.'),(5936,'Payment conditions can be either on a sale/purchase order or on a sale/purchase trade condition document. Payment condition describes the payment conditions that will be applied to an order, such as the payment mode, the term, etc..'),(5937,'An ERP5 Rule...'),(5938,'This portal type is an abstract portal type, so that newTempOrder calls can succeed; one should never have to use this portal type for persistent objects.'),(5940,'An inventory line can be found in inventory documents, and bears the available stock of a certain product reference. There will be one inventory line for each product reference of the inventory.'),(5942,'An Order...'),(5943,'An inventory line can be found in inventory documents, and bears the available stock of a certain product reference. There will be one inventory line for each product reference of the inventory.'),(5944,'An InventoryCell allows to define specific inventory\n      for each variation of a resource in an inventory line.'),(5945,'The inventory module helps the user make a full inventory of the available products in the different warehouses of the company. There will be an inventory line for each product reference that is part of the inventory.'),(5947,'Internal trade conditions are documents that gather all the details of a standard internal order, such as the shipment or payment mode, the tax or discount behaviour. A internal trade condition can be applied to a internal order, and in this case, the information borne by the internal trade condition will be imported to the internal order. This is practical for the user, because it allows not to loose time typing the same information again and again.'),(5948,'Contains Internal Packing List'),(5949,'A Product object holds the information about\r\na manufactured product, like a pen, a bicycle...'),(5950,'A DeliveryCell allows to define specific quantities\r\n      for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5951,'A Product object holds the information about\na manufactured product, like a pen, a bicycle...'),(5952,'Internal Order'),(5953,'Internal Order Line'),(5954,'A DeliveryCell allows to define specific quantities for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5955,'ERP5 default document. Supports synchronisation and XML.'),(5958,'An ERP5 Rule...'),(5959,'An ERP5 Rule...'),(5962,'Une ligne tarifaire.'),(5963,'Container lines bear the different good references included in the container. If three different goods (e-g product references) are in the same container, there will be three container lines: one for each product reference.'),(5964,'A DeliveryCell allows to define specific quantities\n      for each variation of a resource in a delivery line.'),(5965,'Container is the term used in sales packing lists to nominate the container in which the goods will be shipped. The quantity of goods in the container that will be shipped can be different from the quantity of goods that was ordered, and in this case, it will possible for the user to take the action \"Update quantity from container\".'),(5967,'ERP5 default document. Supports synchronisation and XML.'),(5968,'Supply Link defines possible movements of resources between source and destination Supply Nodes. Each Supply Link is associated with one or more industrial phases.'),(5969,'testDeliveryNode'),(5995,'DuplicateInventoryConstraint'),(5997,'